<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nepherites I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 393 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Nefaarud I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nepherites I was the founder of the Twenty-ninth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, ruling from about 399 to 393 BCE. A general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendes">Mendes</a> in the Delta, he overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amyrtaeus">Amyrtaeus</a> of the Twenty-eighth Dynasty, who was probably executed. He kept Egypt independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, sent grain and ships' equipment to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> during its war with Persia, and was buried at Mendes, where remains of his tomb have been excavated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nepherites-i.jpg" alt="Nepherites I" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mario Leonardo Iñiguez · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neferites_sphinx_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
